- Spec anchors: architecture §Standard Contracts (Driver session; Dioxus DOM bridge) and §Established Decisions
  (Driver session; Dioxus integration): fct-t7zq5feb, fct-fltopt6e, fct-6ytdsegs, fct-nl4nv5ny, fct-apdputpm,
  fct-dw3hon6z, fct-ksgwc2yv. Also:
  - security-plan §Input Validation (CLI arguments; Recorded check; Dioxus bridge): fct-4nuyglo3, fct-khxrpkj3,
    fct-frlob5k5, fct-n4q5kc73;
  - obs-plan §4, §6, §8: fct-zuu6oxcq, fct-gwvelgmp, fct-5ydei676;
  - test-plan §3, §5, §10: fct-kzdrls5d, fct-z2ynupl3, fct-mi2j5ztx, fct-glytb3w3, fct-temy7g7i;
  - design-system §Surface: cli (cli-output, cli-graph);
  - layout-templates §Surface: cli;
  - a11y-plan §7: fct-77ewqepn, fct-cbzuzrms.

- **Files:** the base is `8d6c5713`, the parent of the oldest pre-CI commit `54764c41`. `gate.py scope`: `scope: clean —
  changed 19 · listed 18 · recorded 1 (companion 0 · mechanical 0 · in-intent 1 · widening 0) · absorbed 0 · excluded 564`.
  - New (3): `packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/reached.rs` · `packages/escher-driver/src/coverage.rs` ·
    `tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_handler_coverage.rs`.
  - Modified (16):
    - dioxus-native-dom: `src/dioxus_document.rs`, `src/dioxus_document_tests.rs`, `src/element_id.rs` (the one
      recorded file), `src/lib.rs`;
    - escher-driver: `src/replay.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `src/json.rs`, `src/cli.rs`, `src/cli_tests.rs`;
    - seven_guis: `src/session_host.rs`, `tests/cli_commands.rs`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/host_log.rs`;
    - blitz-tests: `tests/stand_replay.rs`, `tests/common/mod.rs`;
    - `docs/capabilities.md`.

- **Guard refusals this chunk met,** each re-issued once in the form the guard passes:
  - implement P2: a `cat >>` heredoc append to `stand_replay.rs` («a cat/tee heredoc with a file target») → the Edit
    tool;
  - implement P3: a recursive `rm` in the smoke's compound, refused by the host's deny rule with nothing run → fresh
    unique dirs, `target/tmp/smk-cov-rec-2229` left standing (gitignored `target/`);
  - wrap P1: a `cat >` heredoc writing a scratch script → the Write tool and run by path;
  - wrap P1: a `rec.py` call piped into `grep` («a pipeline tool's output piped into a filter») → run bare;
  - wrap P1: a `cd` into the chunk's inputs dir («cd … moves the session cwd») → absolute paths.

- **matrix#v030-07** — MET against the diff. `escher-session coverage <app> <check>...` over
  `escher_driver::handler_coverage`; on the six served tasks in both layout modes:
  - `a_snapshot_check_lists_every_handler_the_boot_screen_shows` — exactly `HANDLERS_AT_BOOT`, equal to the graph's
    reading at boot;
  - `a_check_of_each_tasks_drives_lists_its_unexercised_row` — the 7 `GRAPH_DRIVES` tasks;
  - `two_checks_list_only_what_neither_exercised`;
  - `the_load_page_registers_no_state_and_reads_its_click_exercised`;
  - `a_refused_step_exercises_nothing_and_a_keyboard_activation_its_click`;
  - `a_handler_whose_step_removes_its_element_reads_exercised`;
  - through the binary, `cli_commands::coverage_replays_a_kept_check_and_lists_the_handlers_it_left`.
  - The canvas limit is stated in the `command_line` doc, `coverage.rs`'s module doc and `docs/capabilities.md:273-275`.
  - Ledger: `planned → implemented`, ref set (`matrix.py implement`).

- **(security)** MET: ids, owner ids, event names and two counts only; sentinel 0 (`stand_handler_coverage`);
  missing, non-check, over-bound and other-app files refused `malformed`, status 1, no path byte (`cli_tests`,
  `cli_commands`, the P3 smoke).

- **Tests:** unit tests in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the end of the source file (apps/browser/src/about_pages.rs:; apps/browser/src/browser_history.rs:; apps/browser/src/favicon.rs:; apps/browser/src/url_suggestions.rs:; apps/browser/persistence/src/lib.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/util.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/scrollbar.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/fuzzy.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/js_wrapper.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/harness_test.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/mod.rs:); eight unit-test modules sit in files of their own, each a `#[cfg(test)]` child declared through `#[path]` at its parent — dioxus-native-dom's bridge tests, declared at the end of `dioxus_document.rs` as `#[cfg(test)] #[path = "dioxus_document_tests.rs"] mod bridge_tests;`, a child of the module under test so they reach its private fields with no constructor, `pub` or `cfg(test)` shim added (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:), and, since 2026-10-16-file-splits, blitz-dom's `document::changed_set_tests` and `document::font_reading_tests` in `document_changed_set_tests.rs` and `document_font_reading_tests.rs` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:) and escher-driver's `mcp::tests` and `schema::tests` in `mcp_tests.rs` and `schema_tests.rs` (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:; packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs:), each moved out whole with its test paths unchanged;
 each integration test file covers one behavior and opens with a `//!` doc naming the behavior and any guarded bug (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:); regression tests cite upstream issue or PR URLs (tests/blitz-tests/tests/animations.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_interaction_state.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/custom_widget_layout.rs:); documents built with `HtmlDocument::from_html` and a `DocumentConfig` with a `ColorScheme::Light` viewport and `HtmlProvider`, then `resolve(0.0)` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:); scenarios run in both layout modes `for incremental in [false, true]` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:); descriptive snake_case test names (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:); `#[track_caller]` assertion helpers (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:); some tests use `test_that` matchers returning `TestResult<()>` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:); a pointer-event builder is repeated per file (tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:), while the seven_guis stand checks state the tables and helpers they share once, in the module `tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs`, which a check reads by declaring `mod common;` — a module in a subdirectory of the integration-test directory is no test target, so each test-target file still covers one behavior (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:) — and the checks that hold a `Session` — the session checks, the settle check `stand_settle`, the sixteen driver-action checks `stand_act_*`, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `stand_mcp_tools`, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `stand_screenshot_repeat` and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the driver sweep `stand_requirement_sweep`, the served-page checks `stand_cells_served` and `stand_load_page` and `stand_graph`, which also reads `common`'s `GRAPH_DRIVES`, the actions check `stand_actions`, which also reads `common`'s `ACTIONABLE_AT_BOOT`, and the handler coverage check `stand_handler_coverage`, which also reads `common`'s `HANDLERS_AT_BOOT` and `UNEXERCISED_AFTER_DRIVES`, Cells' grid-cell clicks generated by `grid_cells()` rather than stated literally — keep what they share in a second such module, `tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs`, read by `mod session_common;` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:); tests first assert the fixture produces the condition under test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/interaction_state_canonicalization.rs:); WPT test names use forward slashes relative to WPT_DIR (wpt/runner/src/main.rs:); the CI Python tests use `unittest` with one `TestCase` per function (.github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:; .github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:); blitz-tests keeps one test target per file directly under `tests/` — its `[package]` sets no `autotests` — and the one file there that is declared and never built is upstream's single-binary `tests/all.rs`, the manifest's one `[[test]]` table, held at `test = false`: the operator's decision of 2026-10-10, a standing two-line difference from upstream's manifest that `BlitzTestsTargetsTest` pins (tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:; .github/scripts/test_blitz_tests_targets.py:)

- **Unit:** blitz-tests
  - **Path:** tests/blitz-tests
  - **What it is:** Integration tests (tests/blitz-tests/lib.rs:) covering accessibility (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:) and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, the builder's three state attributes on a parsed page — every value of each grammar, on a role that supports the attribute and one that does not, `aria-checked` read on a checkable role alone and neither attribute on a native checkbox or radio, whose `toggled` is written from its checked state under a checkable role and not at all under any other role, a click and a Space moving it, a 5,500-character `aria-checked` nowhere in the tree, 6 tests in both layout modes, run by the workspace test leg, per package and the `stand-repeat` leg (a named `--test` of its list), and the `a11y` CI leg, one of its fourteen named files (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs:); the builder's merged `aria-expanded` · `aria-disabled` · `aria-level` reads, 3 tests (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_merged_states.rs:), the unread `aria-activedescendant` pinned, 1 test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_active_descendant_unread.rs:), and an `inert` subtree skipped by Tab and Shift+Tab, passed through by a hit, absent from the tree and restored when `inert` is removed, a node that holds focus when it comes under `inert` giving focus up with no DOM `blur` or `focusout` and taking no key, the tree's focus reading the window when the focused node was not built, 6 tests (tests/blitz-tests/tests/inert_subtree.rs:), each in both layout modes — the three in the `a11y` CI leg, beside the workspace test leg and per package, `accessibility_active_descendant_unread` and `inert_subtree` also in the `stand-repeat` leg (named `--test`s of its list); block, inline, flex, grid, abspos/fixed and `display: contents` layout (tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/display_contents.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/oof_dynamic_cb.rs:); inline text layout (tests/blitz-tests/tests/whitespace_modes.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/line_break.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_box_baseline.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/br_trailing_line.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_fragment_rects.rs:);
 painting (tests/blitz-tests/tests/background_size.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/svg_background_size.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/outset_box_shadow_shape.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_order.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbars.rs:); paint tree and hit testing, a hit past a node dropped since the last resolve included (tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_tree_incremental.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_events.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_test_dropped_nodes.rs:); input (tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_action.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_selection_anonymous_block.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:); scrolling and fragment navigation (tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:), and an into-view scroll through nested scrolling boxes with the visible-region reader — 7 tests, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scroll_into_view_nested.rs:); a range input's default actions, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction — `range_input_interaction`, 8 tests on parsed pages (6 until 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep), each in both layout modes: the arrows, Home and End stepping a focused range input with one `input` per change, a click setting the value by position and focusing it, degenerate attributes keeping the value finite, bounded and on its grid, a decimal step reading its decimals, a disabled range input taking neither keys nor a click, and attribute writes re-seeding and re-sanitizing the value (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:) and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, removing `value` re-seeding it, removing `step`, `min` or `max` re-sanitizing it, and a `type` change clearing the range data and a change back re-seeding it (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:);
 a scrolled box's own geometry and the hit at a box that clips, since 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit, each in both layout modes — `scrolled_box_client_rect`, 7 tests (a scrolled box's client rect, the nested case, the readers re-based on it and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, a `writing-mode: vertical-lr` box scrolled (70, 120) reading its unscrolled rect, green under both builds), `hit_clipped_at_scrolling_box`, 13 tests (a hit stopped at the padding box of a box that clips by `overflow`, the one-axis case, a `contain: paint` box stopping the hit at its padding box and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the hits at an `img`, inside an `iframe`'s sub-document and inside a filled text `input`, and a box both transformed and scrolled hit where its rows show) and `scrolled_box_absolute_position`, 1 test (a scrolled box's `Node::absolute_position` read where it stands) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_client_rect.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_clipped_at_scrolling_box.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_absolute_position.rs:); `transformed_client_rect`, 4 tests in both layout modes — a translated box, a scaled box and a translated parent's child read where their transforms move them while the child's offset rect does not, and a target inside a translated scrolling box reading inside its visible region (tests/blitz-tests/tests/transformed_client_rect.rs:); style invalidation, transforms, units, transitions (tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/transform_2d_subset.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/rem_after_viewport_change.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:); mutation and leaks (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inner_html_leak.rs:);
 Dioxus integration (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:); `<link>` stylesheet loading (tests/blitz-tests/tests/link_rel_attribute.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:); the seven_guis headless stand — mount, bundled-font text, fresh-boot and incremental identity, offline, one driven interaction per lean task, timer ticks, one stable element id per element (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_boot.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_counter.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_flight_booker.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_timer.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_crud.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:); Dioxus falsy boolean-attribute clearing — `disabled` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_disabled.rs:) and the 28 names of its own list on both attribute paths (the bridge's predicate upstream's 28-name `is_bool_attr` since 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship; `inert` the 28th name the check reads since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, the attribute half only — a truthy `inert` honoured — `inert_subtree`, `stand_keyboard` — and a falsy one cleared by the bridge), a falsy `hidden` leaving the element displayed and a snapshot node (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs.rs:); the snapshot's per-control state through real input, and the password mask on an in-file fixture (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:);
 the stand checks' shared module `tests/common/mod.rs` — no test target and no test in it, the one statement of the per-task tables `controls`, `tab_order`, `INPUT_NAMES`, `rendered`, `LOAD_TAB_ORDER` and `CELLS_TAB_ORDER` (the load page's and Cells' Tab sequences; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:) — joined at 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions by `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` (the flight booker after `return` is chosen on its `flight-type` select, CRUD after a row is selected) and `REGION_NAMES` (`crud-list` → `People`) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:), the stand's drive table `GRAPH_DRIVES` and its `Drive` steps, which drive each conditional write once (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:), and `ACTIONABLE_AT_BOOT`, the measured count of actionable nodes at boot per served task — counter 2, flight-booker 7, timer 3, crud 11, cells 678, load 2 (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:; as measured at escher-0.3.0/chunks/2026-11-08-what-can-i-do-here/report.md), `HANDLERS_AT_BOOT` and `UNEXERCISED_AFTER_DRIVES` — the handlers each served task shows at boot and those each `GRAPH_DRIVES` task leaves unexercised after its drives, Cells' 676 grid cells generated by `grid_cells()` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:) — and of seven helpers — `tab_order` (CRUD six stops, `crud-list` third) and the helper `focused` moved in from `stand_accessibility_ids` and `stand_snapshot_state` since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness — read through `mod common;` by 24 stand checks (`stand_contrast` the eighteenth, since 2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness, `stand_keyboard` the nineteenth, since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, and `stand_requirement_sweep` and `stand_non_lean_tasks` the twentieth and twenty-first, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, `stand_graph` the twenty-second, `stand_actions` the twenty-third and `stand_handler_coverage` the twenty-fourth) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:); since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness the stand keyboard check `stand_keyboard`, 23 tests in both layout modes (11 until 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, which added three and put it in the `a11y` CI leg; the fifteenth the flight type select moving its choice by its arrows; the sixteenth to the twenty-first the load page's stated walk with Enter and Space on its button, Cells' stated walk, Cells' arrows and Enter opening the moved-to cell and its value committed by keyboard, Tab leaving an open editor committing it, a click on another cell committing an open editor to its own cell, and the arrows clamping at the grid's ends and bringing a cell into view: tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:) — Tab and Shift+Tab walking each lean task's stated sequence with wrap, the engine's focus, the snapshot's `focused` and the tree's focus agreeing at every step; Enter and Space on each focused stand button read as its click, 16 rows; the controls HTML gives the keys, a button disabled after it took focus and a button that is itself scrolled, on in-file fixtures; a click focusing each stand button; a `disabled` attribute skipping a form control by Tab and not a `<div disabled tabindex=0>`;
 the CRUD list taking focus and its keys moving the selection; the Apple delete binding on every OS; an inert subtree skipped by Tab; and, since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, the walk beyond boot — the flight booker after `return` is chosen on `flight-type` (five stops, `flight-return-date` joining `back-btn` → `flight-type` → `flight-start` → `flight-book`, reached by Tab and ArrowDown) and CRUD after a row is selected (eight stops), each state reached by keyboard alone and walked in `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` — every `controls(task)` id reached by Tab (an empty set difference against `tab_order` and `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` over every lean task), and Enter and Space on the later-enabled `crud-update` and `crud-delete` each read as its click (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:);
